@page "/Projects/TheJourney"
<div class="ProjectPage">
  <DefaultProjectHeading CurrentProjectURL="Projects/TheJourney" />
  <div class="ProjectDescription">
    <div>
      <h3>Project description</h3>
      <span>
        The first period of school was meant as an orientation phase I didn’t expect an actual programming exercise.
        So this project still caught me off guard. Making a console game with zero experience?
        The goal was to make a little story print in the console where you would make choices by selecting a preordained option.
        But I’m not the type to ever leave a project at the bare minimum requirements.
        Thus the ASCII art for The Journey was born...
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="ImageGrid">
      <img class="first" src="/images/projects/Caroline.png" />
      <img class="second" src="/images/projects/Dave.png" />
    </div>
    <img src="/images/projects/thejourney/TheJourney.gif" />
    <span>
      I used reference images of real people in order to make them.
      I think I spent a good day on each one.
    </span>
    <span>
      After having made three characters I decided that was enough and started working on the code.<a href="#"></a>
      Never since I'd never coded before, there was no strategy for the code beforehand.
      It ended up looking something like <a href="https://github.com/Nx27-ma/BO-textbased-application/blob/main/NodejsConsoleApp2/app.js">this</a> (I'm not putting the whole file here it's wayyy too long).
      Not that pretty in hindsight but it worked.
    </span>
    <span>
      I even made a flowchart for it as I otherwise lost track of the story myself.
      That's how big it ended up being.
      I had a lot of fun working on it.
    </span>
    <img src="/images/projects/FlowChartTheJourney.png" />
  </div>
</div>

